Variable Type Content <code>{eventType}</code> string <code>decision.commande-bloquee</code> <code>{source}</code> string the emitter (<code>process:commande-bloquee</code>, <code>connector-engine</code>, …) <code>{entity}</code> string the ingested table, or <code>—</code> <code>{occurredAt}</code> string ISO timestamp <code>{payload}</code> map, navigable the event's payload — <code>{payload.entity_key}</code>, <code>{#for f in payload.fields}</code> <code>{payloadJson}</code> string the same payload, serialized — for <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> blocks <p>Payloads differ per event type (registry), so guard what may be absent — a missing reference fails the render and the mail is skipped:</p> <pre><code>&lt;h2&gt;{payload.message ?: eventType}&lt;/h2&gt;       {! fallback when the key is absent !}
{#if payload.fields}
  {#for f in payload.fields}&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;{f.key}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;{f.value}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;{/for}
{/if}
</code></pre> <p><code>decision.*</code> payloads come in two shapes, sharing only <code>message</code> — which is why <code>decision-alert</code> leads with it and guards everything else:</p> <ul> <li>Process rules (<code>decision.&lt;name&gt;</code>): <code>message</code> (the rule's   rendered sentence), <code>process</code>, <code>entity</code>, <code>entity_key</code> — and <code>fields</code> (the row columns   the message referenced, with their values) only when the message references any.</li> <li>Dormancy watches (<code>decision.dormant.&lt;workflow&gt;</code>): <code>message</code>,   <code>workflow</code>, <code>doc_key</code>, <code>state</code>, <code>since</code>, <code>first_observed_at</code>, <code>threshold</code> — never   <code>process</code>, <code>entity_key</code> or <code>fields</code>.</li> </ul>
